.TH GEMTEXT 7 "2026-11-09"
.SH NAME
gemtext \- the Gemtext markup format, as read by gemtext2md and its siblings
.SH DESCRIPTION
Gemtext is a simple line-oriented text format.
This page describes how
.BR gemtext2md (1),
.BR gemtext2mom (1)
and
.BR gemtext2pdf (1)
interpret it.
.SH SPECIFICATION
Gemtext is defined by the Gemini project's specification, at:
.PP
.UR https://geminiprotocol.net/docs/gemtext-specification.gmi
.UE
.SH LINE TYPES
These are the line types of the specification.
Each line is interpreted on its own.
.TP
.B =>\ URL [LABEL]
A link.
.TP
.B #\ TEXT, ##\ TEXT, ###\ TEXT
Headings of level 1, 2 and 3.
.TP
.B *\ TEXT
A list item.
.TP
.B >\ TEXT
A quotation line.
.TP
.B \(ga\(ga\(ga
Starts and ends a preformatted block.
Text after the opening marker is an optional description of the block.
.PP
Any other non-blank line is a paragraph.
.SH GROUPING
The specification treats every line as a separate entity and defines no
larger structures except preformatted blocks.
These programs go beyond it in the following way, which is not part of
the specification.
.IP \(bu 3
Consecutive link lines are treated as one list of links.
.IP \(bu 3
Consecutive list item lines are treated as one list.
.IP \(bu 3
Consecutive quotation lines are treated as one quotation, each line being
a paragraph of it.
.IP \(bu 3
Blank lines separate blocks and are otherwise ignored, rather than
being rendered as vertical space.
.SH SEE ALSO
.UR https://geminiprotocol.net/docs/gemtext-specification.gmi
Gemtext specification
